---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="What this site sends — RosterOwl privacy"
  description="Exactly what RosterOwl sends over the network — and what it never sends: your class list. Student names stay in your browser."
>
  <main>
    <h1>What this site sends</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The short version: <strong>your class list never leaves your browser.</strong> Here is the
      complete, checkable list of network activity on rosterowl.com.
    </p>

    <h2>What the site loads</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Its own pages, code, and six font files (three for the screen, three for building your PDFs) — all served from rosterowl.com. No third-party scripts, no CDNs, no trackers, no cookies.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What the site sends</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Nothing containing your data.</strong> After the page loads, the tools work
        entirely inside your browser. Student names, rules, absences, job rotations, word lists
        and charts are processed on your device and stored in your browser's local storage. There is no account system and no
        database.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to verify this yourself</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open your browser's developer tools (F12) and switch to the Network tab.</li>
      <li>Load the seating chart tool, paste a class list, shuffle, download a PDF.</li>
      <li>
        Watch the requests: after the initial page load you'll see no requests carrying your data —
        try it with your Wi-Fi off; the tool keeps working.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>If this ever changes</h2>
    <p>
      Today there are no analytics at all. The one thing we may add is Cloudflare's cookieless
      page-view counter (a script called <code>beacon.min.js</code>) — it counts page loads and Web
      Vitals, sets no cookies, and cannot see anything you type. If and when it's enabled, this
      paragraph will say so in the same deploy. Nothing else gets added without appearing here
      first. This page is the contract.
    </p>

    <h2>Backups</h2>
    <p>
      "Save backup file" downloads your data to your own computer as a plain JSON file you control.
      Restoring reads that file locally. It is never transmitted anywhere.
    </p>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
  main {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-5) var(--page-gutter) var(--space-8);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .lede strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  ul,
  ol {
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
  }
  li {
    margin: var(--space-2) 0;
  }
  li strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  p {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
